c(1, "header lines 1-8; §2.1 table (verbatim); §2.2 table (verbatim)", "positioning", "Habit Check Calendar / 習慣チェックカレンダー (App Store ID 1629764198) by Naoki Otsu, individual developer (com.weeklychecklist) — a weekly grid: rows are habits, columns the seven days of the current week, a tap puts a mark in a cell; tabs and divider lines, a short memo written on the check cell, emoji marks, report view, notifications (present by 2026), backup / restore, CSV export (listed), no habit-count limit, no streaks / goals / nagging; free download with a ~1-week free window then a one-time 'Premium (Pay Once)' purchase; 151 reviews (every one read), 23 storefronts, 2022-06-25 → 2026-09-02, mean 3.748; capabilities (verbatim) " + table("## 2.1 What the product is", 0) + " || listing (verbatim) " + table("## 2.2 The listed model", 0) + " — all 12 polled storefronts list the app as free; the description lists notifications, backup / restore, CSV export, unlimited tabs, 1,000+ emojis, archive, biometrics and dark mode 'with no indication that any of them stops working, or that use is time-limited'; 'It doesn't reward you for streaks, or show you stats, or remind you to do anything. You don't even enter goals into the app. Everything else I tried failed at one of these points… but for what I need it's perfect'", "free week → buy-once $4.99 / ¥780", "mixed", "151 reviews; mean 3.748; JP public 4.6 on 3,151; US 4.81 on 102", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["9490406265","13427992409"])
c(2, "How to read this; Warnings 2, 3, 5, 8, 9; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2; §1.3 table (verbatim); §1.4; §1.5; §1.6; §1.8", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: 106-code taxonomy, every code used; non-exclusive; Wilson 95% CIs on every headline figure; all 151 read in original language (102 Japanese, 38 Latin-script, 5 Chinese, 3 Cyrillic, 2 Korean, 1 Thai), classified by hand with a quoting note, no clustering / keyword / model; files (verbatim) " + table("## 1.1 Files used", 0) + "; coverage (verbatim) " + table("## 1.3 Coverage and reconciliation", 0) + " — 84 storefronts polled, 61 empty; no deduplication needed; 21 validation checks all pass (every 1★ carries a negative code; no grievance code before 2025-01-04; no reviewer both paid and refused); limitations: no version field and no retrievable version history — the paywall date 2025-01-04 is the first review reporting it, a lower bound; only Japan clears 50; one review = 0.66%; no spend data; no verified-purchase flag; 21 reviews (13.91%) are sentiment without product detail; the final six days before extraction effectively unobserved", "n/a", "mixed", "151 read; 1 eligible storefront", "research", "method", "generalisable", ["12642784508"])
c(3, "Warning 1; §1.6 #1; §6.3.2", "data-caveat", "This is a text-review corpus, not a rating corpus: Japan's 103 text reviews sit on 3,151 JP ratings (3.27%); corpus JP 1★ share 24.27% against a public JP 1★ share of 3.11% — 7.8× — 'People who are angry write; people who are content tap a star'; the JP public average is 4.609, barely below US 4.814 and above CA 4.571 — 'The Japanese user population is not unhappy. The Japanese review-writing population is'; public histograms JP 2,424 / 440 / 168 / 21 / 98, US 90 / 7 / 4 / 0 / 1", "n/a", "mixed", "JP text 3.27% of ratings; 1★ 24.27% vs 3.11%", "research", "high", "generalisable", ["12177849705"])
c(4, "§0.1; §3.3 N1; §8.1 #1; §0.8 #1", "must-never-break", "The product is not the problem; the disclosure is: trial grievance union 36 (23.84%, CI 17.75–31.23%, high-priority, mean 1.50, 2025-01-04 → 2026-06-25) — 27 of the 30 1★ (90.00%); TRL_NO_DISCLOSURE 23 (15.23%, CI 10.37–21.82%, mean 1.52; 18 of 23 at 1★, 3 at 4–5★ — 'even people who like the app enough to give it four or five stars report the non-disclosure as a fact worth warning others about'); 14 of them (9.27%) volunteer the fix — say it upfront or sell it as a paid app: 「有料化は仕方無いですが、突然過去の履歴等も見れなくなってしまうのは不親切ではないでしょうか。」; 「良いアプリを継続していくには、利益を出さないといけないので有料版OKです。事前に告知してくれればOKです。けどなぜなんの告知もなく勝手に？」; 'It would be much fairer and more transparent if this limitation were clearly communicated upfront'; reviewers write the copy: 「どうして事前に、「本アプリは有料アプリであり、無料期間終了後、引き続きサービスをご利用になられるには有料プランへの加入が必要です。」とわかりやすく案内しないのだろうか。」; 「１週間しか無料で使えなくて、そのあとは課金です」って書いたほうがいい; the external US and JP listings enumerate every feature and 'contain no statement of a trial, a time limit, or any feature being paid-only'; the most-voted review (5 of 7 helpful, 2★): 'The listing says in-app purchase, not paid app. It isn't a lie, but I can't see it as anything other than deliberate misleading to grow the user base'; of the top 8 reviews by votes 7 are trial grievances; one reports three months, not one week, before the lock (unexplained); §8.1 #1: state the model in the store description and first screen — free for N days, then a one-time purchase, price named", "undisclosed ~1-week trial then lockout", "1★-burst", "trial grievance 36 (23.84%) 1.50; 27 of 30 1★; NO_DISCLOSURE 23 (15.23%) 1.52; SUGGEST_DISCLOSE 14", "must-never-break", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12183022252","12182389221","13883589639","12177849705","13265891866","13620640492","12273751279"])
c(5, "§3.3 N2; §0.6; §8.1 #3, #4; §8.7; §0.8 #2", "product-rule", "Records locked behind the paywall — TRL_DATA_HOSTAGE 6 (3.97%, very strong, mean 1.17; 5 of 6 at 1★) — 'The angriest theme in the corpus'; 人質 (hostage) appears in two independent reviews and a title: 「勝手に無料トライアルを始め、終わったらこれまでつけてきた記録を人質に課金を迫るアプリです」 ('An app that starts a free trial without asking, then when it ends holds the records you've built up hostage and presses you to pay'); separable from disclosure — 'A user who knew about the trial and declined still loses sight of months of their own data'; the app is used for medication adherence (a dose raised every two weeks, 20 / 40 / 100 mg rows: 'I've safely reached and held the final dose') and a 1★ locked out mid-use: 「有料になるなんて思わなくて何飲んでたかメモしておけば良かった。」 ('I wish I'd written down what I'd been taking') — 'A habit tracker used for medication adherence is a clinical-adjacent record. Locking read access to it behind a paywall is a materially different act from locking a feature'; §8.1 #3 never lock read access — let expired users read, scroll and export history forever, gate only new entry and premium features; #4 offer CSV export unconditionally at trial end ('A user who leaves with their data does not write scam'); §8.7 the single highest-leverage change: 'the difference between I decided not to pay and they took my medication log'", "read access to own records locked at trial end", "1★-burst", "DATA_HOSTAGE 6 (3.97%) 1.17", "product-rule", "very strong", "generalisable", ["12174025594","12171233300","12050608960","12670123787","12177849705"])
c(6, "§0.2 table (verbatim); §7.2 tables (verbatim); §7.3 T1, T2; §7.5", "timeline", "The event, dated (verbatim): " + table("## 0.2 The event, dated", 0) + " — zero trial grievances in 51 reviews over two and a half years before 2025-01-04, then 22 in 37 (59.46%); mean 4.43 → 2.78; 1★ from 1 in 2.5 years to 17 in six months; January 2025 alone 17 reviews (busiest month by 2×), 12 grievances, 10 at 1★; before / after (verbatim) " + table("## 7.2 The one demonstrable cause", 1) + " — 'Nothing else in the corpus changed at that date: the praise themes continue unchanged'; T1 it did not end — E3 still 22.22% across 63 reviews over 14 months, the latest grievance 2026-06-25: 'Every new install still meets the same undisclosed wall. This is the difference between a migration cost already paid and an ongoing tax'; T2 ratings recovered to 3.76, still 0.67 below baseline with 12 1★ vs 1 in a period twice as long; whether E3 recovery is a fix or exhaustion of the legacy free base 'matters enormously and the corpus cannot settle it' (the steady 22.22% is weak evidence for exhaustion)", "trial lockout from ~2025-01-04", "1★-burst", "E1 51 @ 4.43 (0%); E2 37 @ 2.78 (59.46%); E3 63 @ 3.76 (22.22%)", "must-never-break", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12145511951","12167354434"])
c(7, "§0.3; §3.3 N5; §5.4 #1", "insight", "The corpus contains a directly measured lost sale: refusals to pay 7 (4.64%, mean 1.29), and several say they were willing to pay until the method changed their mind — 「全ての項目を作って日記がわりにチェックを入れて数ヶ月使用していました。お金払っても良いかなって思っていました。急に「お金払わないと使わせない」と言ってきました。お金払う気がなくなりました。作成側の態度一つで気持ちってこんなにも変わるんですね。」 (4/6 helpful); 「課金も考えたが、このやり方だと先行き不安なので他のアプリに乗り換えました。良いアプリだっただけに残念です。」 — 'a conversion problem caused by presentation, not by price or by product'; churn union 14 (9.27%, mean 1.36) — 6 left for another app or a spreadsheet, 2 uninstalled, 7 refuse to pay, 5 say the developer can no longer be trusted — every one Japanese; one reviewer predicts price escalation ('1200円、2400円…と値上げしていきます')", "surprise lockout", "churn", "PAY_REFUSE 7 (4.64%) 1.29; churn 14 (9.27%) 1.36; TRUST_LOST 5 @ 1.00", "dont", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12670123787","12187124676","12727664598"])
c(8, "§0.4; §2.4; §5.1 table (verbatim); §5.2 table (verbatim); §5.3", "monetization", "The people who did pay are happy and say why: 20 state they bought (13.25%, mean 4.15 vs 3.748; 17 of 20 Japanese); none asks for a refund or regrets the amount; what they name is the one-time model — PAY_ONETIME_PRAISE 14 (9.27%, mean 4.71), 5 prefer it because it is not a subscription (5.00), 10 call the price good value (4.70): 'I hate apps that require a subscription. I love apps that are simple, 1 time purchase, easy to use… Best 3.99 I've ever spent'; 「プレミアムプランをかれこれ2、3年利用しています。…買い切りの部類では安い方だと感じています」; 「Så skönt att det går att köpa appen för en engångssumma!!!」; 「月額とかでは無く、買い切りで広告なしで絵文字も使えるので即日買いました」; payers (verbatim) " + table("## 5.1 Who the paying reviewers are", 0) + " — triggers (verbatim) " + table("## 5.2 What triggers a purchase", 0) + " — several bought immediately (「即購入」 ×4) — 'the buyers were never the ones who needed persuading over a week'; price resistance essentially absent: 1 of 151 objects to the amount ('600円なら他にもいいアプリがありそう'), against 23 objecting to how it was revealed", "buy-once ¥600–1,000 / $2.99–4.99", "purchase-driver", "20 payers @ 4.15; ONETIME_PRAISE 14 @ 4.71; PRICE_HIGH 1", "build-paid", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["13683417986","13862388358","14496901093","11783984084","10843613351","12450403767"])
c(9, "§2.3 price timeline table (verbatim); Warnings 6, 7", "timeline", "The reported price timeline (verbatim): " + table("### The reported price timeline", 0) + " — reported ¥600 (2024-01 → 2026-02), ¥800 (2026-02 → 04), ¥1,000 (2026-06), $2.99 and $3.99 eleven days apart in 2026, while listings show ¥780 and $4.99 — 'Treat this table as reviewer perception, not as a price history'; the free window reported as ~1 week by 21 and three months by one; free / paid vs listing (verbatim) " + table("## 2.3 Free / paid / trial / unclear", 0) + " — ads existed pre-2025 and their removal was a paid benefit; the short memo was free pre-2025 and now sits inside the trial", "price drifted up in 2026", "mixed", "¥600 → ¥800 → ¥1,000 reported", "research", "reviewer-reported", "app-specific", ["10843613351","13683417986","13727748329","13788261701","14196956246"])
c(10, "§2.4; §8.4", "contradiction", "The app's first impression is its best asset and its biggest liability: 「Po otevření aplikace hned nenabízí předplatné a nevypadá to jako další aplikace která je ve free verzi strašně osekaná」 ('On opening, it doesn't immediately push a subscription and doesn't look like yet another app that's horribly gutted in its free version', 5★) — 'The absence of an upfront paywall is what people praise on day 1 and what they call a scam on day 8'; §8.4: disclose the model 'without becoming the thing that reviewer was relieved to avoid — a one-line statement, not a paywall screen'; and consider selling it as a paid app outright — 14 proposed exactly this unprompted", "no upfront pitch; silent lockout at day 8", "mixed", "trial grievance 36 vs pay-positive 26", "research", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["14351890595"])
c(11, "§3.3 N3, N4; §8.1 #2", "dont", "Abrupt lockout and deception vocabulary: TRL_SUDDEN_LOCKOUT 20 (13.25%, high-priority, mean 1.30; 16 at 1★, none 5★) — not a feature gate but a total stop: 「1週間経つとタップすらできなくなります」 ('after a week you can't even tap'); 「課金しなければ全くなんの操作も出来なくなり」 — only one describes a degraded free tier (rows cut back); TRL_SCAM_LANG 12 (7.95%, mean 1.08 — the lowest of any theme with more than one review): 詐欺, 悪質, 腹黒, ミスリード, scam, bait, engaño — 'a brand-risk theme, not a usability theme — it appears in review titles, which is what prospective buyers see first': 「詐欺！」, 「詐欺っぽい」, 「無料アプリのフリをしてる」, 'Paywall scam', 'Demo version'; setup effort framed as deliberate sunk cost (TRL_WASTED_SETUP 4, 1.00); explicit 'don't install' warnings (3); §8.1 #2: show the trial state in-app from first launch — a persistent 'N days left' — 'Converts an ambush into an expectation'", "hard stop at trial end; no trial clock", "1★-burst", "SUDDEN_LOCKOUT 20 (13.25%) 1.30; SCAM_LANG 12 (7.95%) 1.08; WASTED_SETUP 4; WARN_OTHERS 3", "dont", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["13117322780","14222855228","12296229748","12727664598","13953494761","13917364366"])
c(12, "§0.5 table (verbatim); §3.4 P1, P2", "product-rule", "What the app is loved for, in order (verbatim): " + table("## 0.5 What the app is actually loved for", 0) + " — simplicity 65 (43.05%, mean 4.43; UX_SIMPLE 36 with no 1★, UX_EASY 33; 「シンプルで使いやすい」 as a title five times); glanceability 21 (13.91%, 4.95; UX_OVERVIEW 9, every one 5★) — a week × all habits on one screen, no scrolling: 「ブロックの色を埋めていく形式のアプリが多くありますが、これらは項目ごとに場所をとるのでスクロールしないと全ての項目が見れません。このアプリはそれがないので」; the inline memo 9 (5.96%) sits on the check cell: 「メモは格納されずにチェック部分にあるので概観時に一個一個確認せずに済んで…ほんとメモの使いやすさは唯一無二」 — 'the real differentiators, not generic praise'; §8.4 'Do not add complexity' — competitive wins are against apps described as 'overly complicated'", "weekly grid; inline memo", "praise", "simplicity 65 (43.05%) 4.43; glanceability 21 (13.91%) 4.95; UX_MEMO 9", "product-rule", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["13254967446","13427992409","10781563078","14002101328"])
c(13, "§3.4 P5; §2.1 last row; §8.4; §0.8 #10", "product-rule", "The absence of pressure is a reason people choose it: UX_NO_PRESSURE 3 (1.99%, mean 5.00) — no streaks, no goals, no reminders — 'Everything else I tried failed at one of these points'; 'the most commercially important line in this table'; 'Adding gamification would attack the reason this segment is here'; §8.4 / §0.8 #10 do not add streaks, goals or nagging; 4 name the absence of a habit-count limit as why they chose it", "no streaks / goals / nagging; unlimited habits", "praise", "UX_NO_PRESSURE 3 @ 5.00; COMP_UNLIMITED 4", "product-rule", "meaningful", "generalisable", ["9490406265","10781563078","9180394164","11796681292"])
c(14, "§0.6; §3.4 P3", "audience", "It produces a result and is used for medication adherence: outcome_any 26 (17.22%, mean 4.77) — 13 sustained use, 3 strong life-change claims, 9 health uses (medication 5, diet / weight 4, ADHD / rehab 2), fitness 5, study, game dailies, rescue-cat care; 「毎日服用する薬を2週間毎ぐらい掛けて増量していく治療方針だったのですが、飲み忘れる事が多くて初期の投薬量にいつも戻っていました。…薬の項目１つ作って、そこに20mg.40mg.100mgと別々の欄を作りました。…無事に最終の投与量を維持できています。」 — which 'raises the stakes on the lockout'; health uses are all Japanese", "n/a", "praise", "outcome_any 26 (17.22%) 4.77; health 9; OUT_MEDICATION 5 @ 4.20", "none", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12050608960","12171233300","12230886747","14076240245"])
c(15, "§3.4 P4, P7; §5.2 blocker fixed", "tactic", "A specific blocker fixed converts at full price: 「タブが消せないのが難点で購入迷ってました。フィードバックで要望を送りましたが、ちょうど対応中だったのかアップデートで消せるようになっており、即購入しました！」 ('The undeletable tab was the drawback that had me hesitating on buying… an update made them deletable, so I bought it immediately!') — 'That is the template: a specific defect, fixed, converts a hesitant user at full price'; developer positive 9 (5.96%, 4.89) — 6 thank the developer, 3 note frequent updates or a shipped request; one bought purely to thank the developer though the free tier was enough; competitive preference 22 (14.57%, 4.95; COMP_BEST 14, 13 at 5★) from people who tried 'a couple dozen', 'pretty much every habit tracking app', 「ランキング上位から使いました」, 「3年探し続けた」", "fixed undeletable tab via feedback", "purchase-driver", "dev_positive 9 (5.96%) 4.89; competitive 22 (14.57%) 4.95", "do", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12419274643","11783851398","11168885612"])
c(16, "§0.7 table (verbatim)", "data-caveat", "What nobody complains about — eight negative claims tested by multilingual regex with every hit read (verbatim): " + table("## 0.7 What nobody complains about", 0) + " — no one wants a subscription (all 3 mentions favour buy-once), zero refunds / cancellation / chargebacks (structural for a one-time purchase), no current ad complaint, no login friction (none required), no crash / freeze / battery complaint in four years, no slowness ('動作が軽い'), and onboarding complaints are that guidance is absent, never that it is complex", "no login; buy-once", "praise", "0 crashes; 0 refunds; 3 subscription mentions all pro buy-once", "none", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["11783984084","13683417986","14193170527","13862388358"])
c(17, "§3.3 N6; §8.2 #6, #7; §8.6 #3; part 8 #3; §0.8 #4", "must-never-break", "A purchase that does not transfer: PAY_RESTORE_FAIL 2 (1.32%, mean 2.00) — both had already paid: a tablet upgrade that would not appear on the phone, then no support contact found (3★); 'Doesn't let you transfer purchases from one OS to another. Waste of money' (1★) — 'A paying customer writing a 1★ review is the most costly review type there is'; sync requests 7 (4.64%) while one Korean reviewer says iCloud sync does link her devices and the listing claims backup / restore 'even across different devices or operating systems' — capability partial, version-dependent or undiscoverable; §8.2 #6 fix or document restore across devices and OSes; #7 resolve the sync contradiction; research #3: does sync work", "purchase not restored across devices / OS; sync contradicted", "1★-burst", "RESTORE_FAIL 2 @ 2.00; FT_SYNC 7; sync family 8 (5.30%) 3.62", "must-never-break", "meaningful", "generalisable", ["10989685029","13308747446","14193170527","13619450978"])
